<HTML>
@CR
<HEAD>
@CR
<TITLE>_IE_Introduction ('basic')</TITLE>
@CR
<STYLE>body {font-family: Arial}</STYLE>
@CR
</HEAD>
@CR
<BODY>
@CR
<table border=1 width=600 id='table1' cellspacing=6 cellpadding=6>
@CR
<tr>
@CR
<td>
@CR
<h1>Welcome to IE.au3</h1>
@CR
IE.au3 is a UDF (User Defined Function) library for the 
@CR
<a href='http://www.autoitscript.com'>AutoIt</a> scripting language.
@CR
<p>  
@CR
IE.au3 allows you to either create or attach to an Internet Explorer browser and do 
@CR
just about anything you could do with it interactively with the mouse and 
@CR
keyboard, but do it through script.
@CR
<p>
@CR
You can navigate to pages, click links, fill and submit forms etc. You can 
@CR
also do things you cannot do interactively like change or rewrite page 
@CR
content and JavaScripts, read, parse and save page content and monitor and act 
@CR
upon browser 'events'.<p>
@CR
IE.au3 uses the COM interface in AutoIt to interact with the Internet Explorer 
@CR
object model and the DOM (Document Object Model) supported by the browser.
@CR
<p>
@CR
Here are some links for more information and helpful tools:<p>
@CR
Reference Material: 
@CR
<ul>
@CR
<li><a href='http://msdn1.microsoft.com/'>MSDN (Microsoft Developer Network)</a></li>
@CR
<li><a href='http://msdn2.microsoft.com/en-us/library/aa752084.aspx' target='_blank'>InternetExplorer Object</a></li>
@CR
<li><a href='http://msdn2.microsoft.com/en-us/library/ms531073.aspx' target='_blank'>Document Object</a></li>
@CR
<li><a href='http://msdn2.microsoft.com/en-us/ie/aa740473.aspx' target='_blank'>Overviews and Tutorials</a></li>
@CR
<li><a href='http://msdn2.microsoft.com/en-us/library/ms533029.aspx' target='_blank'>DHTML Objects</a></li>
@CR
<li><a href='http://msdn2.microsoft.com/en-us/library/ms533051.aspx' target='_blank'>DHTML Events</a></li>
@CR
</ul><p>
@CR
Helpful Tools: 
@CR
<ul>
@CR
<li><a href='http://www.autoitscript.com/forum/index.php?showtopic=19368' target='_blank'>AutoIt IE Builder</a> (build IE scripts interactively)</li>
@CR
<li><a href='http://www.debugbar.com/' target='_blank'>DebugBar</a> (DOM inspector, HTTP inspector, HTML validator and more - free for personal use) Recommended</li>
@CR
<li><a href='http://www.microsoft.com/downloads/details.aspx?FamilyID=e59c3964-672d-4511-bb3e-2d5e1db91038&amp;displaylang=en' target='_blank'>IE Developer Toolbar</a> (comprehensive DOM analysis tool)</li>
@CR
<li><a href='http://slayeroffice.com/tools/modi/v2.0/modi_help.html' target='_blank'>MODIV2</a> (view the DOM of a web page by mousing around)</li>
@CR
<li><a href='http://validator.w3.org/' target='_blank'>HTML Validator</a> (verify HTML follows format rules)</li>
@CR
<li><a href='http://www.fiddlertool.com/fiddler/' target='_blank'>Fiddler</a> (examine HTTP traffic)</li>
@CR
</ul>
@CR
</td>
@CR
</tr>
@CR
</table>
@CR
</BODY>
@CR
</HTML>
